commit 91a48ebc699a9bcdee1c40a3964f74be0fe96667
Author: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>
Commit: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>

    exp11: the unavailable path is the degenerate interval and nothing else
    
    Hardening of the exp_11 cell: `exp11_cell` re-raises a convergence refusal whose
    interval has positive width, so only the zero-width cancellation the plan
    registers becomes a defined `unavailable` statement and any other fault of the
    frozen helper aborts loudly. An empty cohort is refused before anything is
    resampled -- the void rule always reaches it first inside this module, and a
    caller that bypassed the rule would otherwise reach a bare TypeError.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

