commit 824dce98c758ed3011a79445aea253b500c6676e
Author: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>
Commit: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>

    exp11: R1 historical rows, copied under a source-field map
    
    Plan section 4 round 1, item 2(b), R1. `historical_rows` re-reports five rows
    from exp_06's and exp_09's canonical records under the registered source-field
    map: C - D and D - A from the descriptive `D` list (diff, nominal_two_way only),
    C - A from H1 and C - F from H1b (diff, two_way, convergence, verdict), E - A
    from exp_09's E1 (those plus category and non_inferior_at_margin).
    
    Rows are selected by contrast / room / metric assertions, never by list
    position; a source whose selector matches twice is refused. Extant fields are
    copied exactly with their original names, meaning and interval convention, an
    absent requested field is refused, and every other decision-bearing field is
    null and named in `not_recorded`. Each row records the source path, that file's
    sha256 and its selector; a missing source, or a summary.txt that is not the
    bytes the record's own summary_sha256 binds, is refused. Nothing is recomputed
    and no descriptive row becomes a decision.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

commit bc8e7622af5254db07943f0bf99b999b16e3599c
Author: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>
Commit: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>

    exp11: three screen families under exp_11's suppression
    
    Plan section 4 round 1, item 2(b), S1. `exp11_screens` runs one eleven-cell
    Bonferroni family per declared contrast (G - D, C - G, G - E), keyed by the
    contrast itself, so the adjustment protects within a family and nothing is
    claimed across the three.
    
    `exp11_screen_cells` wraps the historical `screen_cells` -- called unchanged --
    with exp_11's universal void/unconverged suppression: a cell the invalidity
    policy voids or the convergence check refuses carries no label, and records the
    reasons. This gate is exp_11's own; exp_06's and exp_09's screens keep exactly
    the semantics they registered (asserted side by side on the same data).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

commit 968e16775307506f645719a711b93a8c0f5ef859
Author: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>
Commit: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>

    exp11: the four-arm interaction cell N1i
    
    Plan section 4 round 1, item 2(b), N1i. `interaction_rows` assembles the cohort
    of (G - E) - (D - A) once over all four arms: every arm paired against the first
    with exp_02's own index / ir_path / protocol assertions, ONE mask finite across
    the four arms and the three seeds, each arm's original exclusions reported.
    `interaction_void_reasons` adds the >= 99 % joint-cohort rule and keeps the
    component checks of G - E and D - A, each named by its component.
    
    The estimate is the frozen bootstrap's `paired_intervals(g - e, d - a, clusters,
    seeds)`, so the interaction is resampled jointly and its covariance preserved;
    two independently bootstrapped intervals are never subtracted. Cancellation
    gives a zero-width interval, which the frozen helper refuses and `exp11_cell`
    reports as `unavailable`.
    
    `exp11_decision` dispatches a registered decision to the two-arm or the four-arm
    assembler; its category is read as "positive = larger heading-frame penalty
    after yaw pretraining", never as harm by any single arm.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

commit fff7948d037ca9cc235f2a84a67ca3ceb1334d5a
Author: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>
Commit: Yixun-Hu <yixunhu21@gmail.com>

    exp11: the decision notation of plan section 3, generically
    
    Plan section 4 round 1, item 2(b), the notation block. `decision_fields` writes
    each statement of section 3 as its own field of one contrast X - Y at margin m:
    category (two-sided, h2_label's semantics), y_non_inferior_at_margin (-L < m),
    x_margin_advantage (U < -m) and equivalent_at_margin (95 % containment). The
    direction is the cell's own `contrast` string; every inequality is strict, so an
    endpoint on a boundary establishes nothing; a margin-bearing field without a
    margin is refused.
    
    `exp11_cell` applies it to one cell: exp_06's invalidity policy and convergence
    gate, a `status` instead of a pass/fail `verdict` (exp_11's decisions are the
    statements, not a margin verdict), every field withheld when the cell is void or
    unconverged, and a *defined* `unavailable` result when the interval is degenerate
    -- the frozen bootstrap helper's zero-width refusal is caught here rather than
    aborting the summary or being weakened in the helper.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

