    exp11: pipeline init yawaug_hf (arm G, heading frame)
    
    Plan section 4 round 1, item 1. Arm G is exp_04's yaw-augmented SimpleViT
    (exp_09's initialisation) fine-tuned in exp_06's HEADING frame, so:
    
    - init_of gains `yawaug_hf` with the same ${EXP09_YAWAUG_CKPT} checkpoint and
      the default heading frame the function resets on every call, so a mixed
      queue of E and G gives each job its own frame;
    - the APPROVALS_PY identity resolver (exp_04's approved checkpoints.aug,
      through the finalizer) now answers for both inits that start from it;
    - child_log takes the prefix orientation_cue_fairness_haa for an exp_11
      record root, so no exp_11 queue writes oriented_cyl_ or yawaug_haa_ logs.
    
    Bare `zeroshot` keeps its historical exp_06 expansion; `yawaug_hf:zeroshot`
    is G's own zero-shot set. No behaviour of the exp_06 or exp_09 queues changes
    (their dry runs are asserted byte-for-byte).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

